WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.420 --> 00:00:04.210
With a run time clocking in at over three
hours, it might be easier to explain what

00:00:04.210 --> 00:00:07.100
doesn't happen in Avengers: Endgame instead
of what does.

00:00:07.190 --> 00:00:08.800
For instance, fans don't get bored.

00:00:08.960 --> 00:00:10.540
Fans don't get up to use the bathroom.

00:00:10.800 --> 00:00:12.559
And fans don't ever want it to end.

00:00:12.560 --> 00:00:15.930
But it did end and we're here to explain what
that ending was all about.

00:00:16.180 --> 00:00:20.380
Here's the ending of Avengers: Endgame explained...with
lots of spoilers ahead.

00:00:20.900 --> 00:00:24.580
After returning from their various missions
to different past moments from the history

00:00:24.590 --> 00:00:28.949
of the Marvel Cinematic Universe, the Avengers
grouped back up with the six infinity stones

00:00:28.949 --> 00:00:29.580
in tow.

00:00:29.720 --> 00:00:33.840
But Black Widow was missing, as she sacrificed
herself to retrieve the Soul Stone.

00:00:33.840 --> 00:00:37.600
It all goes down in a scene that mirrored
the death of Gamora in Avengers: Infinity

00:00:37.600 --> 00:00:38.100
War.

00:00:38.140 --> 00:00:41.979
The new and improved Professor Hulk who has
the combined might of the Hulk with the intellect

00:00:41.979 --> 00:00:46.589
of Bruce Banner used the recreated Infinity
Gauntlet to reverse Thanos' snap, bringing

00:00:46.589 --> 00:00:50.160
back all the people who were erased from existence
in Avengers: Infinity War.

00:00:50.300 --> 00:00:52.800
But though he tried, it couldn't return Natasha
to life.

00:00:52.960 --> 00:00:57.079
It may seem weird that a guy with an all-powerful
wishing glove still couldn't undo this one

00:00:57.080 --> 00:00:57.720
major death.

00:00:58.129 --> 00:01:01.600
But Black Widow's absence at the end of the
film proves that the Infinity Stones aren't

00:01:01.600 --> 00:01:03.680
quite as infinite as their name would suggest.

00:01:03.900 --> 00:01:07.420
Of course, that doesn't mean our heroes can't
find a way to pluck her out of the past and

00:01:07.420 --> 00:01:08.020
send her...

00:01:08.420 --> 00:01:09.940
"BACK TO THE FUTURE!"

00:01:11.060 --> 00:01:12.740
Okay, so here’s where things get weird.

00:01:12.920 --> 00:01:16.740
On their trip back to 2014 to get the Power
Stone seen in the beginning of Guardians of

00:01:16.740 --> 00:01:21.291
the Galaxy our timeline's Nebula was captured
by Thanos, who secretly replaced her with

00:01:21.300 --> 00:01:23.520
the evil 2014 version of Nebula.

00:01:23.729 --> 00:01:28.380
Having infiltrated the Avengers headquarters,
evil Nebula then summoned 2014 Thanos and

00:01:28.380 --> 00:01:29.980
his armies using the time machine.

00:01:30.080 --> 00:01:34.399
They blew everything up, with evil Nebula
getting ahold of the new Infinity Gauntlet

00:01:34.400 --> 00:01:36.220
in a callback to the original comics.

00:01:36.260 --> 00:01:40.480
But then the good Nebula from the real timeline
shot her younger evil self stone dead.

00:01:40.490 --> 00:01:43.229
Luckily, this didn't affect the good Nebula
at all.

00:01:43.229 --> 00:01:44.289
So what does that mean?

00:01:44.289 --> 00:01:48.509
It proves our heroes' pasts can't be changed
and that alternate universes are probably

00:01:48.509 --> 00:01:51.700
something the MCU is going to need to sort
out in Phase 4.

00:01:52.060 --> 00:01:56.360
With the Infinity Gauntlet once again in play,
the Avengers fought Thanos to a standstill,

00:01:56.369 --> 00:02:00.659
including an absolutely epic sequence where
Captain America gained the powers of Thor

00:02:00.659 --> 00:02:05.049
by wielding the mystic hammer Mjonir 
to deliver a massive whooping, something which

00:02:05.049 --> 00:02:07.780
was first teased way back in Avengers: Age
of Ultron.

00:02:07.909 --> 00:02:11.819
Still, Thanos eventually called in the cavalry
by which we mean the intergalactic horde of

00:02:11.819 --> 00:02:14.310
creeps we saw back in Avengers: Infinity War.

00:02:14.310 --> 00:02:18.680
Luckily, the Hulk's reverse snap had also
restored all the dusted heroes from Avengers:

00:02:18.680 --> 00:02:19.180
Infinity War.

00:02:19.180 --> 00:02:23.200
Just as Captain America was about to face
the armies of Thanos alone again echoing a

00:02:23.209 --> 00:02:27.340
classic moment from the comics all the dead
heroes arrived via Doctor Strange's magic

00:02:27.340 --> 00:02:30.769
portals in a scene reminiscent of the end
of Ready Player One.

00:02:30.769 --> 00:02:31.760
Only… better.

00:02:32.020 --> 00:02:35.940
Plus, the arrival of all the heroes allowed
Captain America to finally deliver the team’s

00:02:35.950 --> 00:02:40.069
signature catchphrase from the comics, "Avengers
Assemble!," something fans have been waiting

00:02:40.069 --> 00:02:44.220
for for the last decade, especially after
Marvel did a fakeout tease at the end of Age

00:02:44.220 --> 00:02:44.880
of Ultron.

00:02:50.400 --> 00:02:51.260
"Avengers…"

00:02:51.840 --> 00:02:55.940
In the end, you knew it had to come down to
Tony Stark versus Thanos for the fate of the

00:02:55.940 --> 00:02:56.480
universe.

00:02:56.580 --> 00:03:00.000
After all, the showdown had been teased way
back in Avengers: Age of Ultron.

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:04.040
And luckily, Tony was clued in to his big
chance because Doctor Strange was there to

00:03:04.040 --> 00:03:04.720
give him the finger.

00:03:04.820 --> 00:03:09.720
No, not that finger just an index finger to
note that this was the one chance in 14 million

00:03:09.720 --> 00:03:12.800
for victory that he had foreseen in Avengers:
Infinity War.

00:03:12.900 --> 00:03:17.340
Stark didn't disappoint, taking the Infinity
Stones from Thanos and using it to snap the

00:03:17.350 --> 00:03:20.560
big purple meanie out of existence along with
all his minions.

00:03:20.560 --> 00:03:24.159
We learned in Guardians of the Galaxy that
mere mortals cannot harness the power of the

00:03:24.160 --> 00:03:25.260
Infinity Stones, though.

00:03:25.360 --> 00:03:28.380
Fulfilling that cosmic promise, the strain
was too much for Tony.

00:03:28.480 --> 00:03:32.900
He died a hero, and was given a hero's funeral
attended by everyone who was anyone, including

00:03:32.900 --> 00:03:35.880
Nick Fury and even that kid from Iron Man
3.

00:03:36.020 --> 00:03:40.180
As for why it had to be Tony who saved the
day and bit the dust well, he's the guy who

00:03:40.180 --> 00:03:42.920
started the whole MCU back with the first
Iron Man movie.

00:03:43.160 --> 00:03:46.890
He's been the heart and soul of the franchise,
and without Tony making the ultimate sacrifice

00:03:46.890 --> 00:03:49.430
to save the universe, it just wouldn't feel
right.

00:03:49.430 --> 00:03:51.300
He may be gone, but he'll never be forgotten.

00:03:51.320 --> 00:03:52.360
"I am Iron Man."

00:03:54.760 --> 00:03:58.900
Following Tony’s funeral, Captain America
was tasked with returning the Infinity Stones

00:03:58.909 --> 00:04:03.129
to their proper places in time, in order to
ensure that no more alternate universes were

00:04:03.129 --> 00:04:03.700
created.

00:04:03.800 --> 00:04:07.819
But in a big twist, Cap decided not to come
back from his time travel jaunt.

00:04:07.819 --> 00:04:12.300
Instead, he returned to the 1940s so he could
finally have that dance he promised Peggy

00:04:12.300 --> 00:04:14.200
Carter back in Captain America: The First
Avenger.

00:04:14.260 --> 00:04:18.900
And then he stayed there, apparently marrying
her and living a long and full life.

00:04:18.900 --> 00:04:19.860
"Peggy."

00:04:19.860 --> 00:04:21.700
"I'm going to need a raincheck on that dance."

00:04:21.700 --> 00:04:22.200
"Alright.

00:04:22.200 --> 00:04:24.280
A week next Saturday, at the Stork Club."

00:04:24.280 --> 00:04:26.630
So Steve Rogers, at least, got a happy ending.

00:04:26.630 --> 00:04:28.730
And so did his buddy Sam Wilson, a.k.a.

00:04:28.730 --> 00:04:29.360
The Falcon.

00:04:29.420 --> 00:04:33.440
Not only was he brought back to life, but
an old Steve Rogers still spry at well over

00:04:33.440 --> 00:04:38.440
100 turned up to present Sam with his indestructible
shield and the charge to carry on as the new

00:04:38.440 --> 00:04:42.720
Captain America — a development that also
took place in the comics several years ago.

00:04:43.260 --> 00:04:46.980
Tony and Steve might be gone, but one of the
Big Three may apparently still be moving forward

00:04:46.980 --> 00:04:47.720
in the MCU.

00:04:47.980 --> 00:04:51.520
After wallowing in self-pity throughout the
whole film, Thor finally seemed to get his

00:04:51.520 --> 00:04:55.320
act together at the very end and decided to
head into space with the Guardians of the

00:04:55.320 --> 00:04:59.220
Galaxy, leaving Valkyrie behind as the new
leader of the Asgardians.

00:04:59.450 --> 00:05:03.200
We also got a hint of what we might see when
Thor and the Asgardians of the Galaxy return

00:05:03.200 --> 00:05:07.540
in Guardians of the Galaxy vol. 3, as their
final scene showed Peter Quill searching for

00:05:07.540 --> 00:05:12.170
the location of the 2014 version of Gamora,
who came through the portal with Thanos...but

00:05:12.170 --> 00:05:13.680
vanished after the final battle.

00:05:13.900 --> 00:05:17.560
But that's just one of several loose ends
Marvel will have to tie up in future movies...

00:05:18.060 --> 00:05:21.800
We won't have long to wait to see the fallout
from Avengers: Endgame, as the teasers for

00:05:21.800 --> 00:05:26.420
Spider-man: Far From Home suggest Peter Parker
and Happy Hogan will be dealing in very different

00:05:26.420 --> 00:05:27.940
ways with the loss of Tony Stark.

00:05:28.100 --> 00:05:30.240
They aren't the only ones with things to work
through though.

00:05:30.380 --> 00:05:34.760
After stealing the Tesseract again Loki got
a second chance at life that seems likely

00:05:34.760 --> 00:05:39.140
to be explored in the upcoming Loki series
on Disney's new streaming service, Disney+.

00:05:39.140 --> 00:05:43.790
Likewise, Hawkeye has his family back, which
is likely to be explored in the upcoming Hawkeye

00:05:43.790 --> 00:05:45.580
series on the same service.

00:05:45.580 --> 00:05:48.570
Meanwhile, Wakanda suddenly has its king back
again.

00:05:48.570 --> 00:05:51.710
That's probably one king too many, though,
because whoever's been running the show for

00:05:51.710 --> 00:05:55.880
the last five years in T'Challa's absence
M'Baku maybe? might not want to just hand

00:05:55.880 --> 00:05:56.880
the throne back over.

00:05:56.960 --> 00:06:00.920
And then there's Black Widow, who has a solo
film in development even though she's dead.

00:06:00.930 --> 00:06:03.490
Will the heroes rebuild a time machine to
bring her back?

00:06:03.490 --> 00:06:04.860
Will the film be a prequel?

00:06:04.900 --> 00:06:07.940
Will we find out she was a Life Model Decoy
the whole time?

00:06:08.140 --> 00:06:09.440
So many possibilities...

00:06:09.560 --> 00:06:12.520
All told, the Avengers saved a lot of lives
and won the day.

00:06:12.720 --> 00:06:14.000
But that was the easy part.

00:06:14.000 --> 00:06:16.200
Picking up the pieces is likely to be the
hard part.

00:06:16.200 --> 00:06:19.780
And we can't wait for Phase 4 to begin so
we can see just how they do it.

